> (first-order language, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"dab75c9f48db057d\" href=\"?note=dab75c9f48db057d\" title=\"17-df-first-order-language\">17-df-first-order-language</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi,\\psi,\\chi\\in\\mathrm{Form}_L\">\\(\\varphi,\\psi,\\chi\\in\\mathrm{Form}_L\\)</span> (formulas, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"465b5002eb16d1cf\" href=\"?note=465b5002eb16d1cf\" title=\"17-df-formula\">17-df-formula</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Ax}_{\\mathrm{Prop}}(L)\">\\(\\mathrm{Ax}_{\\mathrm{Prop}}(L)\\)</span> (set of propositional axiom instances, defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{Ax}_{\\mathrm{Prop}}(L)\\coloneqq\n\\bigl\\{&amp;\n\\varphi\\to(\\psi\\to\\varphi),\\\\\n&amp;(\\varphi\\to(\\psi\\to\\chi))\\to((\\varphi\\to\\psi)\\to(\\varphi\\to\\chi)),\\\\\n&amp;(\\neg\\varphi\\to\\neg\\psi)\\to(\\psi\\to\\varphi)\n:\\varphi,\\psi,\\chi\\in\\mathrm{Form}_L\n\\bigr\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{Ax}_{\\mathrm{Prop}}(L)\\coloneqq\n\\bigl\\{&amp;\n\\varphi\\to(\\psi\\to\\varphi),\\\\\n&amp;(\\varphi\\to(\\psi\\to\\chi))\\to((\\varphi\\to\\psi)\\to(\\varphi\\to\\chi)),\\\\\n&amp;(\\neg\\varphi\\to\\neg\\psi)\\to(\\psi\\to\\varphi)\n:\\varphi,\\psi,\\chi\\in\\mathrm{Form}_L\n\\bigr\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This atom contains only propositional Hilbert axiom schemes. Quantifier axioms and generalization belong to a chosen first-order deduction system, not to the propositional axiom set.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remar